221	This Remington EP-1000 Smooth & Silky Hair Removal System works great. I use all the time. My hair would grow so quickly in the past that I would have to shave every few days. Now after repeated use of this epilator i could go for well over a week sometimes two and people don't notice. However here are some tips:    Bottom line there will be discomfort as you began to use it. Hello - You are ripping your hair out. Some reviews in the past read it doesn't hurt... But at most (this is coming from a person who had always shaved)... It hurt at first but then some areas actually tickled.. lol.. Others stung big time but was done right after the hair is pulled. But I promise after repeated use you will get used to it... I am a person that doesn't take pain well... So I am being honest here.     Second... Use it after a hot shower so then your hair will be easy to remove. It does a great job removing the smallest haris. It an area hurts more... pull your skin so it is tight and continue use. Afterwards, apply lotion.     Because your hair grows in spurts you will have to redo the missed spots  within the next few days... But this is very quick... and rather painless since you got the intial step done.     Afterwards- keep it up. You will reap the rewards! For awhile this product was out of stock... I am glad it is back again. I would totally buy this one again because it is well worth the price.     Oh another tip: Be sure to ex-foliate every so often... Because you hair will be getting lighter and thiner as you use this product.    Otherwise, I totally recommend the product. You'll have less hair. No more bumps or dark hair showing... I have used it everywhere but my underarms and my upper lip (I think it is too small of an area and I rather just wax) And the results are the same. It is worth it. Sure I still shave every once in awhile... But I wouldn't go without my Remington. :)	\N	0	POSITIVE	5	0	\N	221	132	\N	\N
