446	I messed up like 20 times with the upper tray alone and I kept reusing the tray until the final product came out perfect!    Quality was excellent and the whitening product stayed inside and both were very comfortable  :)    BEFORE YOU START:  I suggest you youtube \\\\"dental trays\\\\" and click on the video with the dentist, an older gentleman.  He helped me a lot with how to mold them to your teeth properly.    Even though the thing comes with instructions and I read them and tried to follow along, they don't really work well so I made a couple of tweaks and this is what worked for me!      TIPS:   Now you must use the water as soon as it comes to a boil, because I found that the trays melt more and mold better to your teeth when using the water at its boiling point.      *WATCH THE youtube VIDEO to see how melted they are suppose to be before you place it in your mouth to mold*    CAUTION:  GENTLY SHAKE OFF EXCESS BOILING WATER SO YOU DON'T BURN YOUR GUMS & MOUTH.  After shaking, the tray is never hot it's just soft enough to mold.  But work quickly because the tray dries up fast.    The boiling water is only good for about 30-60 seconds.  I kept boiling the water again and again to remold.  Don't be afraid to remold the tray,  I messed up sooo many times and it always worked.  Even if they trays end up sticking together its not the end of the world. RE-Dip in boiling water until it gets soft and open the parts that stuck together.    My finished product looks like I got it right the first time.  The tab at the top accidently got stuck to the front of the mold and I was soo sad but I just dipped it in boiling water and then pulled it from the front.  It didn't break off or anything and it looked like it never happened. lol!    The bottom tray I messed up a couple times because there was too much teeth showing in the front of the tray so I just dipped it back in boiling water and waited until tray was soft.  Once ready to mold, I would just mold tray back to its original state with my fingers.  I had to Redip like 3 times.  Then I was ready to mold it in my mouth again.      You don't have to be an expert to do it. Just don't be scared and have lots of patience.    I could have stopped at the second re-mold but I'm a bit of a perfectionist.     I'm very pleased with the product.  Thank you so much. :)	\N	1	POSITIVE	5	1	\N	446	132	\N	\N
