e the company, it's products and chairs.  The price of $200 is fantastic but no panacea for the overall score.<br /><br />Customer Service: 3 stars - When I phoned in to return my order the representative was pleasant on the phone, asked me my name, how my day was going and got down to business.  I can't really knock them for following the book on the shipping and restocking fee, but had they gone \\\\"above and beyond\\\\" I would have marked this area with higher stars.  They were not rude, they were trained and three stars is a good review (just not great)<br /><br />Overall: 2.8 stars (round up 3) - I certainly wanted to mark this product as two stars but in the efforts of integrity and going off my grade sheet I must round up to three stars which says this product gets an OK mark.  I don't like that, I honestly think that had customer service stepped up and credited the shipping or at minimum the restocking fee this would have left me with a pleasant experience.  I've owned several OSIM chairs and TRULY was ready to step up to the human touch (even marked my calendar for their arrival at my Costco) but this experience shows me how far Brookstone / OSIM were willing to go with their chairs and the efforts that Human Touch would make.  The foot & calf massager would be an excellent purchase for those looking for better blood circulation in their legs, but not for those that crave the uPhoria feeling (OSIM) of a good calf/foot massager., it's products and chairs.  The price of $200 is fantastic but no panacea for the overall score.<br /><br />Customer Service: 3 stars - When I phoned in to return my order the representative was pleasant on the phone, asked me my name, how my day was going and got down to business.  I can't really knock them for following the book on the shipping and restocking fee, but had they gone \\\\"above and beyond\\\\" I would have marked this area with higher stars.  They were not rude, they were trained and three stars is a good review (j