2059	I work with tiny things in a lab. After a visit to my dentist, who was wearing this brand of glasses (although a different model), I decided to buy a pair for my lab. Everything is as described, and the quality is high. However, when I am working it tends to be with a small object on a waist-high counter, causing me to look almost straight down. Because these glasses are fairly heavy, they tend to slide down my nose and fall off my face. This requires the use of the included headstrap to hold the glasses on.<br /><br />The other factor that one should carefully consider is the magnification and working distance. The higher the magnification, the longer the working distance. More importantly, the higher the magnification, the more sensitive the focus is to the distance from the object. I opted for the 5x ocular, which has a fairly long working distance - perhaps a bit too long for me. The narrow depth of field makes it challenging to maintain my head at the correct distance, while working, to keep things in perfect focus. This is no fault of the seller or the product. It's just physics. In retrospect, I should have opted for a shorter working distance.	\N	0	POSITIVE	4	0	\N	2059	132	\N	\N
