2710	Our daughter is now 2 1/2 years old, and we have owned one of these since she was 2 months old (I'm just now getting to review ALL the stuff we bought on Amazon, so, I've got some mileage into our baby products).  I can remember how scary it was being a first time parent and hearing about SIDS and the like.  It's especially unsettling to hear the ever-changing rhythm of a newborn's breathing and not know if that's what they are supposed to sound like or not.  When I found this product I could not wait to get it home (I think I even paid for the 2 day shipping, I was so excited).  When we received it I tested how effective it was in a few different scenarios.  The idea is that if the sensor pad feels no movement (i.e. breathing) for 20 seconds it sounds the alarm (an alarm loud enough to hear on a different level of ANY average home).  So, the standard test is to take the baby out and wait.  It worked.  Then I set a pedestal fan about 4 feet away from the baby and set it to high and took her out (I did this with both our crib AND her bassinet).  The alarm went off. Great.  So, then I took the fan out of the equation and just did some walking in the area of the crib and bassinet to see if that was enough to register a movement with the sensor and trick it onto thinking the baby was breathing.  No dice, the alarm sounded.  I tried the same thing with a heavy toy in the bed, in case weight was a contributing factor, and the alarm still went off when there was no baby.  This thing really works, and works well.  The engineer in me was satisfied that we got what we were looking for in any scenario: peace of mind so we could finally sleep without worry.  Even my anti-baby-technology parents we relieved to have the system on the bassinet when they were babysitting (my father was visibly happy when we asked how things went when they were looking after her, because, as he said, they had confidence that if something went seriously wrong they would know right away and that was reassuring).     By the way, the batteries last forever, so I LOVE that this system is not dependant on a plug and is so portable.  It even becomes a good deterrent to the roaming toddler who just got their \\\\"big kid\\\\" bed.  You'll know very quickly if your little one is having a solo adventure at 3AM!  I would recommend this to every parent of a newborn.  I just can't say enough good things about it (they even have a co-sleeper on the manufacturer's website that is compatible with this system, in case you don't use a bassinet or crib!).  If we are gifted with a second child I plan to even try one of the diaper clip movement sensors (last I checked they were mainly a UK item).  It seems like a great thing to have when you are away from home and the baby wants to nap:)	\N	6	POSITIVE	5	7	\N	2710	132	\N	\N
