3808	I have had these now for about a year.  I am tough on glasses, so i tend ot have a bunch of them.      These are not bad.  They are cheaply made.  Within 3 months, one pair popped a lens.  It won't stay in anymore.  The others are OK though, so for the money, they are good.    The key item here is the bifocal is not gradient and low on the glasses.  So if you want a bifocal where you have to look sharply down or tilt your head back to see magnified that is great.  But if you are doing something that requires prolonged straight ahead viewing, then these are NOT the glasses for you.    Glasses are good for:    1. Reading.  2. Driving (you can see through the clear glass forward and see magnified when you look down at the dash or radio, standard for far sighted folk like me).      Glasses are terrible for:    1. Use on computers.  Your neck gets stiff tilting your head back to magnify the screen.  2. Television (if you need magnification for TV).    I also find that no matter how I adjust these, they slide down my nose. That is annoying because then you have to look even further down to get the magnification so I have to keep pushing them back up.    Overall, OK reading glasses.  The lens is clear and the magnification is right.  And the hinges make them better than the cheap models.  Quality of the product is so so, and that is the ultimate reason for my 3 star rating.  If you want nicer glasses, there are much better brands out there.  I have numerous other sets I like better than these, that are comfortable, lighter, rest easier and more firmly on the nose, etc.    I won't buy them again, but I ain't throwing them out either.	\N	4	NEUTRAL	3	5	\N	3808	132	\N	\N
