3890	There are things that can help someone who is having a seizure, putting something in their mouth is not one of them as jaw and face muscles may tighten during a seizure, causing the person to bite down. If this happens when something is in the mouth, the person may break and swallow the object or break their teeth!<br /><br />Don't worry - a person can't swallow their tongue during a seizure.<br /><br />If the person is lying down, turn them on their side, with their mouth pointing to the ground. This prevents saliva from blocking their airway and helps the person breathe more easily.<br /><br />During a convulsive or Tonic-clonic seizure it may look like the person has stopped breathing. This happens when the chest muscles tighten during the tonic phase of a seizure. As this part of a seizure ends, the muscles will relax and breathing will resume normally. Rescue breathing or CPR is generally not needed during these seizure-induced changes in a person's breathing.	\N	1	NEGATIVE	1	1	\N	3890	132	\N	\N
