4249	I have been using this facial steamer for several months. I previously used the \\\\"pot of boiling water on the stove with a towel draped over my head\\\\" method. Well, I decided that wasn't too safe when one time a towel caught fire on my gas stove! This product is a much better method, as it keeps only a small amount of water at the perfect temperature for facial steaming (without scalding your skin) ... and it never catches fire, lol!    When I ordered the facial steamer, I had terrible adult acne. It included about every blemish problem on the spectrum, from small blackheads and small to large whiteheads, to particularly troublesome newly developed cystic acne. I had painful, embarrassing large cysts on my face. I did not have poor hygiene or eat a bunch of chocolate, or any of the other stereotypical myths regarding the causes of acne. The only thing I could find that it had a causal link to was stress. It was completely ruining my quality of life, like psoriasis and other skin diseases often do.    Anyways, I first used the full facial steamer attachment as part of my routine skin care regimen, after regular cleansing with soap and water. This steamer attachment gives your entire face a very nice, relaxing steam facial, and the attachment is well-designed as far as its shape, so that it's comfortable to use and rest your head on.    The unit has a timer, which came in very handy because at first I had to start with shorter steams and gradually increase my steam facials up to longer ones. I think the timer has increments from like 2 or 3 minutes up to 15 minutes, and then it automatically shuts itself off.    Then, while my pores were open from the steam facial, I would use any microdermabrasion cream from the drugstore with the microdermabrasion tool. This tool isn't shown in the product picture, but it's basically a hand-held tool with a switch that allows you to select if the attachment on the tool turns clockwise or counterclockwise. It comes with a brush attachment and a sponge attachment. I would evenly apply the microdermabrasion cream to my face and put a little bit on the brush attachment, and let the tool gently exfoliate all the impurities that had just been steamed out of my pores, along with dead skin cells, etc., that had just been softened and loosened through the steam facial. This home microdermabrasion tool is fantastic! Just be careful not to overdo it. I would use it for maybe one or two minutes at the most, and there's no need to press down on your face ... just let the tool do the work for you.    Then I would splash cold water on my face to close the pores (also very invigorating), and then applied toner with a cotton ball, and then my favorite moisturizer with the sponge attachment of the microdermabrasion tool. I'd use the sponge attachment with moisturizer for another minute or two, and let me tell you, boy did I ever feel pampered when I was done!    I could see a VERY positive effect on my \\\\"run-of-the-mill\\\\"-type acne (smaller blackheads and whiteheads) within one week, and this system pretty much eliminated it after two weeks. By that time I was taking 11- to 15-minute facial steams. As a wonderful side effect, my use of the system also helped me relax and reduced stress, which, as I mentioned would make my problem worse.    Then came the best part, which is what I think is best thing about this Conair product. After I got rid of the smaller problems, I then started using the smaller cylinder steamer attachment that allows you to target certain parts of your face with the steam, such as just the forehead, or just one side of the face or the other, etc. I guess it's supposed to be used for sinuses, but I used it to really target those awful, nasty acne cysts.    When I used the smaller attachment, I kept a cold washcloth handy to periodically calm the cysts during the steam facial. Although it was somewhat painful to have the gross, deeply-embedded, infectious pus steamed out and brought to the surface of my skin, unfortunately that is exactly what needed to happen so that I could then exfoliate using the microdermabrasion tool, and then purge it (carefully, with either clean tweezers or clean fingers). Again, I would follow up with a splash of cold water, then toner, and then moisturizer using the sponge attachment just as before. The cysts were completely gone within another couple of weeks.    This all-in-one product is a complete home facial system since it includes the microdermabrasion tool and the steamer, as well as the two attachments for both parts of the facial. This system was quite literally a lifesaver for me! I had been to numerous dermatologists, and tried countless other remedies, including Retin A, Accutane, vitamin B6, and just about every other \\\\"cure\\\\" under the sun - pharmaceutical, homeopathic or otherwise. Using this Moisturizing Mist Microdermabrasion & Facial Sauna System, I went from not wanting to leave my house due to my appearance to having completely clear skin within a month.    I no longer need to be as vigilant as I was when I first bought the facial steamer (when I was using it at least four or five times a week, if not every day) but I do continue to use it on a weekly basis for a wonderful, relaxing facial and microdermabrasion treatment in the privacy of my own home. It saves me a ton of money and continues to keep my skin in peak condition.    I highly recommend this great system from Conair to anyone with acne, and I imagine that if it worked this great for a person with severe skin problems, that it probably works just as well for people without skin problems. If I were wanting to buy one, I would try to find this kit anywhere, and I definitely couldn't live without mine! I wouldn't have taken the time to write all this if I didn't feel that strongly about it!	\N	1	POSITIVE	5	1	\N	4249	132	\N	\N
