6039	I have owned this trimmer twice.  The first I bought locally and when it stopped holding a charge after one week, I returned it to the store for a replacement.  The second one has lasted and served me well for a year now and I really like the T-blade and overall functionality of the trimmer, but the battery now will barely hold a charge long enough for a single trim.  This is the result of a cheap charger that does not properly condition the cheap NiCad battery pack.  This is a common problem with all NiCad batteries (as well as NiMH to a slightly lesser degree). They really require a good electronic conditioner/charger that will measure the remaining charge and drain the cells the rest of the way to empty before initiating the charging phase.  This is the only way they will last.  Anyway, you're not going to get that in a $25 trimmer, so I am retiring mine and will switch to a cord/cordless model so that when the battery is done, at least I can still use it plugged in.	\N	5	NEUTRAL	3	5	\N	6039	132	\N	\N
