6087	One known design flaw of the Rota-dent is the hole in the bottom of the handle where the charger plugs in. If this hole gets exposed to moisture over time (which is bound to happen), the contacts corrode and the toothbrush will either stop working or it will no longer charge. This happened to my unit in 6 months and it had to be replaced. The \\\\"lifetime warranty\\\\" will cover this problem only once (they say this is misuse and corrosion is not covered under the warranty). <br /> <br />The Water Shield was designed to protect your investment in this very expensive toothbrush. It is constructed of highly durable PVC which is custom formed to slip over the base of the power handle and completely seal out water, moisture, and any material which may find its way into the charging hole in the base of the toothbrush and cause corrosion or a short. <br /> <br />As it says in big bold letters in the instruction manual \\\\"NEVER DRENCH, SUBMERGE, OR IMMERSE POWER HANDLE IN WATER\\\\". That is a funny demand for an item that is bound to get wet! Try using an electric toothbrush without getting the handle wet! Even rinsing the head after use is likely to get a drop of water running down the handle. Keep it in the stand (which you pretty much have to as it won't stand up on its own) and that drip of water goes right down to the hole where the charger plugs in, the toothbrushes most vulnerable spot. All it takes is a tiny spec of moisture combined with the electrical current flowing through the dissimilar metals of the charging connector to start the corrosion process. It took 6 months for my Rota-dent to stop working completely due to this corrosion problem. <br /> <br />Other quality electric toothbrushes (Braun Oral-B, Sonicare, etc) have fully waterproof power handles which use inductive chargers so there are no electrical contacts to corrode. This is a huge design flaw of the Rota-dent and one of its only major flaws. Based on brushing performance, the Rota-dent is truly one of the best electric toothbrushes on the market; it's the mechanical engineering design that is very poor. <br /> <br />I have used my replacement power handle with the Water Shield for a year now and the charging connector still looks like brand new! I don't have to worry about the unit getting wet anymore. I don't even dry it off after use! <br /> <br />I have owned just about every electric toothbrush on the market, and this one does the best job of keeping your teeth clean and gums healthy. Being an engineer, I had to provide a solution to this corrosion problem. The Water Shield is highly durable and easily slips over the base of the power handle between charges. Every two weeks, when the power handle requires charging; dry the handle, slip the Water Shield off, charge the unit in a dry place, slip the Water Shield back on, and enjoy the peace of mind that your Rota-dent is protected! <br /> <br />You can get these on Ebay, search for Rota-dent...	\N	13	NEUTRAL	3	15	\N	6087	132	\N	\N
