6521	I have had both SVT and Atrial Fib.  Since you can have this device with you almost everywhere (doesn't need to come out your bag going through airport security) it is easy to capture a rythmn which just won't show up in the doctors office.  After you know what you have and with just a litle ECG education from your doctor, this device will let you know what is going on.  If you want to print or email your recordings the software works just fine, but is not always intuitive.  Some reviewers have complained that the thumb contacts don't work and it is true that for some people it doesn't. I have let 20(or so) people try it and there have been 3 or 4 who just can't get a reading, 3 or 4 who need to use their fingers instead of their thumbs, 3 or 4 who get usuable readings (but noisy) and about half who it just works for.  In any case everyone can hook up the cable to adhesive electrodes on your forearms and get perfect readings.  I myself get good readings with my thumbs, but always use the cable when sending a tracing to my cardiologist-they are just less noisy.  Also, when using a computer there is a 2x button in the included software that magnifies the amplitude by 2 which makes it much easier to read (printed, emailed or computer screen only).  This is my second portable ecg.  I first had the \\\\"read my heart\\\\" from the same company.  Both work the same when using a computer, but this one is much more convenient as you can see the tracing on the lcd screen.	\N	0	POSITIVE	5	0	\N	6521	132	\N	\N
