6650	I have been using ear candles for years, Wally's is my favorite brand, and they do work! I'm taking the time to write a review to help offset all the negative ones here.  About 10 years ago, I went to a natural healthcare practitioner and had her candle my children's ears.  I watched what she did, and since then have been doing it myself.  The wax in the candle when you are finished IS earwax - with each of the six of us there is a different color, consistency and amount of  wax drawn out by the candle.  Some people may be mistaking the fluffy, light-colored matter in the candle for supposed wax - as I understand it that stuff is there to help keep the hot, liquid wax from running back down into your ear while candling.  I used a brand without that kind of lining once and the wax did run back inside my son's ear.<br />If you've positioned the candle correctly and no wax is drawn out, my experience has been that you either: a) need a couple of drops in your ear first to loosen things up (ear oil, alcohol, whatever you're comfortable with) or b) need a second candle on the same ear.  I suppose it could be that you don't have any excess wax at the time, but we've never had that happen.  We don't ear candle often, a few times a year at most.<br />BTW - I can't speak to the quality of service from this seller - I've always gotten these at a local grocery store.  But this price is pretty good and I'm going to order a couple of packages.	\N	3	POSITIVE	5	3	\N	6650	132	\N	\N
