7740	I give workshops and presentations on biofeedback and I own two of these gauges.  They are rugged and seem to be accurate.  The precision is measured out to the tenths decimal place.  While I think this meter is a bit expensive for what you get, it is a useful tool for monitoring skin temperature on the hands.  The relative changes are a good indication of what is happening in the nervous system from moment-to-moment.  In a nutshell, hands warming up are good.  Hands cooling down usually indicates stress and sympathetic nervous system activation.  While this is a very simple device, it is quite useful for those learning to quiet the mind and provides real time feedback to know if what you are doing is working and to what degree (pardon the pun)!  They also make combination GSR and temperature meters which are definitely a step up.  If you are really serious about stress management biofeedback for in the home then I would also read my reviews of FREEZE FRAMER and HEALING RHYTHMS.  They go a lot further and I think they are both well worth the cost.	\N	10	POSITIVE	4	10	\N	7740	132	\N	\N
