7926	After having my corded razor die a slow death, my wife went out 3 Christmases ago and got me one of these shavers.<br />  And it is one of the BETTER razors out there for the price. If you can find it cheaper, though...by all means get one!<br />  Let's face it, if you don't have a million-dollar face, why blow several hundred for a shaver that will do the job AS WELL for a lot less?<br />  The Remington MS2-200 does a very good job, and although when fully charged, sounds like a steroid-laden hornet in heat, still comes through with flying colors. It has one of the ebst trimmer units around.<br />  My only \\\\"complaint\\\\" is that the head foils wear out sooner than my old Braun foils did. While directed to replace the foils every SIX MONTHS, I think that's asking a bit much. And at $14+ a shot every time I replace them, it adds up.<br />  After a few years, this razor will cost more than a hundred bucks!<br />  Thankfully, the cutting heads (when kept clean) last for more than a year (recommended changeout).<br />  You can get about 10 GOOD shaves per charge (over the 3 minute limit), and although you get a full charge after several hours, you can get one \\\\"fast\\\\" charge in less than an hour, so that's not bad at all in a pinch.<br />  If you don't use the shaver EVERY DAY, then you can eek out a few more months on the foil heads (10-12 months).<br />  I would shop around online for better prices for the foils. Some places sell both the heads AND the cutters, when all you need are the HEADS.<br />DO your homework, and save a few bucks.<br />  Overall, it's not a bad unit, but I am dreading the day when the rechargebale battery needs replacing, and how difficult THAT will be.<br />  Time will tell.<br /><br />Bob G.	\N	2	POSITIVE	5	2	\N	7926	132	\N	\N
