9160	We had a beach vacation planned, but before we left, our son broke his arm.  We got a waterproof cast with the thought that he could wear it in the ocean.  After the cast was put on, however, the doctor warned us that he should avoid the ocean to avoid getting sand in the cast.  If there was sand in the cast, the doctor said, it would be dangerous when the cast was sawed off -- the grains of sand would cause serious danger. <br /> <br />This was a big blow to us.  In desperation I searched the internet and found the Xerosox.  We ordered one somewhat skeptically and tried it out in the local pool.  Wow, it worked!  The cast cover works by creating a vacuum seal over the arm (or leg).  We half expected the water to leak in where the cover sealed against the bare skin on his arm.  However, it worked!  His arm was dry -- no leakage.  The only dampness was from sweat (his cast vented sweat at the elbow, and that was a tad damp, but not where the cover sealed on the skin). <br /> <br />We took the Xersox cover to the beach, and it worked beautifully.  Each day our son was out in the rolling Atlantic surf.  Three days the surf was quite wild -- it would knock you down and kicked up a lot of sand, that type of thing.  Our son had no trouble with the cast cover, even on those rough-water days.  We also didn't worry.  We could tell at a glance that the cover was sealed and that the vacuum hadn't leaked.  Once his cousin accidentally knocked the valve to the cast cover open, but we quickly resealed it and could tell by looking that the vacuum seal on the arm had not been broken. <br /> <br />The only hardship, if you can call it that, is that the cast cover should be loosened periodically to reduce the tightness on the arm.  The directions say you should loosen it once every 45 minutes.  We pushed this to an hour and had no ill effects.  I did have to wear a waterproof watch to keep track of the time, but that was no problem.  We'd get our son out, rinse our hands, loosen thecover, let the arm rest a minute, then reseal the cast in the Xerosox and send our son back into the water. <br /> <br />Today my son had his cast changed, and he had a glowing report from doctor and technicians.  The Xerosox satisfied everyone -- my son, us, the medical personnel.  I'd recommend Xerosox to anyone.	\N	25	POSITIVE	5	25	\N	9160	132	\N	\N
