9368	My main motivation in getting the ShadowBlast stick was to simplify my morning makeup routine and possibly find a quick and easy eye shadow product for when I go on vacation. The smoky eye part was nice, but not really my primary reason. I actually don't follow Cover Girl's technique to the letter. I do apply the lighter shadow over my lid and brow bone, followed by the darker one in the crease. But I also like to blend in a little of the darker shadow on the outside of my lid.  Now I do use liner under the bottom lashes, so I hoped maybe I could use the tapered end as a liner. That did work for about a week, but after a while the taper wore down and grew a bit blunt (much like lipsticks do) so it no longer \\\\"lined\\\\" very well. So if you line the upper lid as they suggest, you'll most likely eventually have this problem.<br /><br />But despite this issue with the liner tip wearing down, I do like the application process. The eye shadow is very blendable and layers well. At first it can be a bit difficult as it feels like using a crayon on the face. But after a few uses the ShadowBlast stick warms up and doesn't tug on the skin like it did with the first few uses. I did find that I had to apply quite a bit if I wanted an intense smoky look. But for my everyday wear, I did go with a lighter hand and I loved the ease of use. I do recommend using an eye shadow primer. Not only did this improve wear, but it also eliminated the bit of creasing I had when I used a bit heavier hand.<br /><br />What surprised and disappointed me the most was the amount of shimmer in ShadowBlast. I usually envision the smoky eye look to have more a darker matte eye shadow with perhaps a bit of shimmer on the brow. The darker shadow isn't as bad, but the light has way too much, and as a result, I found myself using more of the brown shadow on my lid, with only a little bit of the taupe shadow on the inner corners.<br /><br />Another issue I had with ShadowBlast was that twice it has broken on me! If you're not careful and twist out too much of the shadow, it can break very easily, especially during the summer months when the product gets warmed up and becomes softer. It first happened on my Bronze Fire stick. Then it happened again with Purple Plum.  I'd like to see an applicator that doesn't twist so easy, so as to prevent people like me from twisting out too much product. I also had issues with the lids cracking and breaking on me. To say I've had loads of bad luck with this product is an understatement.! If you're not careful and twist out too much of the shadow, it can break very easily, especially during the summer months when the product gets warmed up and becomes softer. It first happened on my Bronze Fire stick. Then it happened again with Purple Plum.  I'd like to see an applicator that doesn't twist so easy, so as to prevent people like me from twisting out too much product. I also had issues with the lids cracking and breaking on me. To say I've had loads of bad luck with this product is an understatement.	\N	1	NEGATIVE	2	1	\N	9368	132	\N	\N
