10105	When it comes to telescopic back scratchers, I have yet to find one I consider decent.  Most of them are the pen-sized model, which is suitable for light scratching only, and it's barely functional at that.  This one is sized to be more robust, but it is still not nearly as good as it could be.    There are three issues I have with this unit.  The most serious problem is that, like most telescopic scratchers, it's too flimsily constructed.  The tubing is too thin, and made of inferior metal, so when extended, the scratcher flexes way too much.  It's not strong enough to be anything more than a delicate scratcher.  I would rather this item be twice as heavy, if it meant it was sturdy, but alas, it is not so.  The description claims \\\\"sturdy construction\\\\".  Don't believe it.  I've seen firmer celery.    The second issue I have is that the prongs are not long enough.  Sure, you look at the photo, and it looks like it should be fine.  What isn't immediately obvious is that pretty much the *entire* width of the rod segments are BELOW the top of the scratcher head.  Which means that the tubing gets in the way of most of the length of the prongs.  This translates into an inability to scratch any area of your back where you don't have a really good angle.  If you don't have the flexibility to put your arm way behind your head, you're going to have parts of your back you can reach, but can't scratch.    The third issue is the ball bearing they put at the base of the handle.  If they had just made it a one-piece metal cap with a smooth and rounded end, it would have been perfect.  But they tried to get fancy and give you a ball bearing instead.  This means that not only do you have to contend with the sharpness of the edged rim, but you also run the possibility of catching hair or skin in the bearing.  No thanks!      So, the final judgement is that as far as what telescopic back scratchers *should* be, this is quite lousy.  However, given how poor the quality of available telescopic scratchers are, this one isn't too bad by comparison.	\N	1	NEGATIVE	2	2	\N	10105	132	\N	\N
