10462	We used to have a traditional 4 wheeled stroller system from Graco, the one with small wheels. Those traditional strollers are, IMHO, meant for malls only and are very difficult to maneuver on anything but pavement i.e. they are terrible for parks or beaches or cobblestones etc. With this background, we were looking for a jogging stroller with large wheels for \\\\"off-roading\\\\" since we are not really joggers.  After much research, we decided on this Schwinn Jogger. Bear in mind that this is actually made by inStep (instep.net) but I never compared the inStep and Schwinn joggers.      Pros:  =====  - Silky Smooth and effortless to push  - Works like a dream on grass and sidewalks  - Very easy to turn  - Great in Malls/stores etc  - Front Wheel can be locked in place but we have not done that since we do not use for jogging  - Very Easy to fold  - Great brakes  - Adjustable Handle      Cons:  =====  - VERY big when folded. Don't even think about buying this if you have sedan. I have a Honda Pilot it takes up half the cargo space when folded!  - When folded, the front suspension scrapes against the road scratching it  - Tiny Cargo basket. For such a behemoth, they have a tiny cargo basket and an average sized diaper bag barely fits in it. It can be argued that it is after all a jogger which negates the need for a basket but since they did provide a basket, it does not make any sense for the smallness of it  - Once folded, there is nothing to lock it in place, no latch to keep it together or any thing to lift it. It is just a hassle to fold this thing , then lift it in a bear hug to put it in the car all the while hoping it would not just plop open in your arms  - The sun shade does not move. It cannot be moved, say, to cover the baby from front if you want to shade the kid from light from a setting sun  - Tires are NOT airless though I do not think I would pump them more than 4-5 times a year  - The bottle holder is too shallow, IMHO and a water bottle can just fly out ofit on a bump  - There is no cover for the paremt tray which is just asinine for a jogging stroller. This WILL be a major pain    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~    Don't let the cons scare you though. I will recommend this to a friend, a friend with an SUV not a sedan and given another chance will buy it again. The most important thing in a stroller is the comfort of your child and our daughter seems very comfortable in it. Plus the handling off road with no shocks transferred to the kid make it up for the bulk.	\N	1	POSITIVE	4	1	\N	10462	132	\N	\N
