11180	We read positive reviews about this wheelchair on other sites, and decided to buy it while we were waiting for our daughter's much more expensive special needs transport chair to get covered by insurance and delivered.  This is an ideal transport chair, as it has the telescoping handles that make it easy for a parent to push.  It's a sturdy, well made chair.  The wheels are great for a sidewalk, or even rougher terrain, and I love the little wheels on the back to prevent the chair from tipping over.  Our daughter is 6, 45 inches and 56 pounds, and this fits her great.  Her feet barely touch the foot rests, so she will be able stay in it for at least 2or 3 years.  I read another review by a parent of a 3 year old, and it also fit that man's son. The legs rests make it comfortable even if a kid's feet don't touch the foot rests. I don't think this would be ideal for a kid who needs to wheel himself, as even though the arm rests can flip back out of the way, it's a bit awkward like that.  Our daughter mainly needs us to push her, so that's not an issue.  She *can* wheel herself, but it wouldn't work well for doing that constantly, because the arm rests kind of get in the way when they are back, and bump under her arms when they are down.  Again, this is only an issue if a smaller child needs to wheel himself. This chair folds up nicely, and the leg rests pop off to make it smaller - all you have to do is lift the lever to get them off.  Considering my daughter's transport chair/stroller costs over $3000 - I think this is a great value for the price!  If a child doesn't need any special head or trunk support, this chair is perfect!  I'm glad we bought it and we continue to use it often even though she has another transport chair (the other one is in my trunk, this one is in my husband's, so we use it about half the time).	\N	8	POSITIVE	5	9	\N	11180	132	\N	\N
