11713	Excellent for PTTD troubles. Did help a great deal ... but: you will have to wear two pairs of socks. 1 for beneath the brace and one OVER the brace because the Velcro catches on to your pants leg. This means your foot will be too wide to fit in anything but a lace-up sneaker that is one size larger than your regular size. The brace inflates a sack below your arch, lifting the arch which alleviates one of the problems with PTTD. The brace also keeps you from pronating which is also a problem with PTTD.  DON'T buy a Small size unless you are very petite or child-size.  I ended up buying one for the other foot which helped me walk better, helped me heal faster. Wearing one made me feel lob-sided. I am finding a bit of skin irritation from either the heat of all that wrapping, or the material of the brace.  The brace is worth buying but I hope you are not in a hurry. Check the shipping dates.  UPDATE JAN 2012  Another reviewer wrote about how these will stink. I can't get the smell out and they are falling apart.  My doctor put me in an immobilizer, a soft cast, up to the knee. He said PTTD needs complete immobilization. My ankle feels better. Maybe you should save your money and buy an immobilizer.	\N	2	NEUTRAL	3	4	\N	11713	132	\N	\N
