12000	I purchase a lot of things on Amazon, but don't  often leave reviews. Not because I'm not happy with items, but i guess I'm just too lazy. But i HAD to leave a review on this razor. This is my very first DE razor. I've been looking at them a long, long time, and envisioning accidentally slicing myself to bits, and just the thought of it freaks me out. But i took the plunge and boy, I'm so glad i did. I love this razor! I am in love with this razor! I want to marry this razor and have like 10 thousand of its babies!<br /><br />In case you are wondering, I'm a girl and am using this razor on my legs, underarms and other bits. Here's a little history. I have very, VERY sensitive skin. I cannot use disposable razors as they irritate my legs way too much. I've been using a Schick Hydro 5 for a long time, because it was one of the only razors that didn't cause me to get a rash after using. The Hydro is good for what it is. But the blades are so expensive. I did tons of research on DE razors and different brands of blades. I thought that for my sensitive skin, the Merkur Futur adjustable with the Personna blades would be the right combo. Today was the first day that i tried my Merkur  out. I received it the day before yesterday, but just stared at it for two days because i was too scared to use it. I was terrified when i started using it today, but it wasn't scary at all in the end. And I've gotten the best shave of my life with this razor and the Personna blades. I shaved my legs early this morning and they still feel silky smooth. Even though i used the number 1 setting. I can't imagine the shave I'd get if i used the 5 setting. I'd probably get friction burns on my femur.<br /><br />One word of warning about this razor. Be very, VERY careful when you are inserting the blades. And when adjusting the razor. I thought i was being careful, but apparently i wasn't careful enough because i have a deep gash on my thumb from where my finger slipped off the top and slid right across the blade. That was not fun. But everything else about this razor is. Here's how i shaved. I put a light oil on my legs. Then i used shaving soap and applied it with a badger brush. I used short strokes and was careful to not press the razor into my skin. I just let the weight of the razor do the work. It was such a great experience that i actually can't wait to shave again! The only \\\\"downside\\\\" is that it took three times longer to shave with this razor than my old one. But that's because i was so anxious and didn't want to go faster and end up cutting myself. If you've been wanting to try out a DE razor, but have been scared like me, take the plunge! I don't think i could ever go back to even my trusty Hydro 5 after my tryst with the Merkur Futur!	\N	4	POSITIVE	5	5	\N	12000	132	\N	\N
