12790	[[VIDEOID:b9ff01fc837b993b5bcec65f413fb09f]]This is a handy and simple to use medical analysis tool.  It operates on two AAA batteries and it measures your pulse and your blood oxygen level.  It comes with a nice carrying case with a Velcro flap closure.  On the back of the case is a belt loop and a plastic ring for a carabiner (Carabiner not supplied). It also comes with a nice neck lanyard so you can easily carry it without using your hands and you know where it always is.<br /><br />It comes with a nice bright display that is easily read and you can rotate the readings by pressing the power button. To take a reading:<br />* Insert your finger<br />* Press the power button<br />* Hold your finger still<br />* If you need to then press the power button to rotate the displayed readings.<br /><br />Taking a reading is fast and easy.  My wife's mom developed a very bad case of pneumonia last winter and actually was sick for months.  She had trouble breathing and we got her an oximeter to monitor her O2 levels in her blood and she kept a record of it for the doctor.  If it went too low she went to the hospital.  Readings below 90% are considered low and when she got to 86% it was time to go to the hospital and be checked out.  At 88 years old you don't mess around with pneumonia.  Low blood O2 levels can cause damage to your body, dizziness and fainting.  We went through that with her illness.<br /><br />This is a good product and it worked well.  I rated it at 5 stars.<br /><br />I was supplied a sample for test and evaluation. A review was not promised to the supplier in exchange for the sample but I stated that if I provided a review that it would be fair and honest.	\N	8	POSITIVE	5	9	\N	12790	132	\N	\N
