13575	I just received delivery of this chair a few days ago (from the maker of the chair)<br />and thought I would write a review since I did not see any reviews on Amazon for this<br />specific model (Human Touch Ijoy 2720). My initial impressions: WOW!<br />To my understanding, this is currently the largest massage chair in the Ijoy series.<br />I really have to give this chair a very high rating and I am very glad I made the purchase.<br />The chair offers a very deep, invigorating massage consisting of four different modes:<br />kneading, rolling, percussion, and compression. The chair allows you to pick any one of<br />the aformentioned modes, or, it has 3 automatic modes i.e. \\\\"back refresh\\\\" which consists<br />of a 15 minute massage incorporating all four of the featured massage styles.<br />I believe I read some reviews of the Ijoy 2850 of which some people complained it being<br />a little on the small side, but I have to tell you that is not a concern in this model.<br />I'm 5 foot, 8 inches tall and this chair is plenty big! It is 35 inches wide, and when<br />fully reclined, spans 57 inches.<br />I researched this chair and the company, Human Touch, and read many articles/reviews that<br />this is a great company who makes quality massage chairs.<br />What is also great about the chair is it doubles as an excellent recliner. Its so comfortable<br />you could spend hours reading, watching TV, or just relaxing in it.<br />Other features include a swivil out cup holder, and a power jack to plug in low voltage<br />items such as a smartphone or Ipad. The chair also has a built in roller so you can<br />easily transport it around a room or even move it to another room.<br />It cost about one third to one fourth less than some of those other massage chairs. Ok, so what's<br />missing then? Many of the more expensive chairs feature airbags under your behind or around your<br />legs and feet which adds to the cost, as well as reclining into an anti-gravity position.<br/>But again, I want to emphasize, for anyone looking more for an invigorating massage all the way down<br />to your very lower back up to your neck and head area, this chair does an excellent job. In fact, the<br />kneading massage has to be felt to be believed.<br />I also purchased the matching Human Touch foot/calf massager ottoman (HT 1355, and its very nice because it<br />swivels over and doubles as an ottoman.<br />Do not be concerned about the massage not being strong enough. It has a cushion padding which can be removed<br />for a stronger massage and it was so strong, it almost hurt, so I put it back in.<br />In summary, for anyone looking for a deep tissue massage covering the neck (and yes, it really massages the neck<br />nicely), upper back, middle back, and lower back, this is the chair to get.<br />One of the best purchases I've made. Remember too, you can later add a matching foot/calf massager i.e. HT 1355.<br />I highly recommend this massage chair.	\N	17	POSITIVE	5	17	\N	13575	132	\N	\N
