13591	I have substantial hearing loss and have found typical phones very difficult and frustrating to use because of their general lack of volume.  After looking and looking for an amplified phone that also included all the basic phone features, I was pleased to discover this Krown model.<br /><br />I haven't had the phone long, but so far I am impressed.  The phone gets VERY loud, and tone, volume, and \\\\"boost\\\\" amplification are all adjustable to your specific needs.  No more frustration because you can barely hear a caller with this phone.  It also has an adjustable, extra-loud ringer to help avoid missed calls.<br /><br />The Starplus-45 also has all the features you want on a phone today, with backlit LCD, caller ID, mute, hold, and speakerphone functions.  I looked at other amplified phones on the market and had a hard time finding one with all of these features.  The Krown delivers it all with solid construction too.<br /><br />Note: Some photos of the phone show the handset with nothing printed on the back of it.  In fact, the back of the handset has \\\\"LOUD USE WITH CAUTION\\\\" printed on the top by the earpiece.  It is not particularly obtrusive, but it is there.<br /><br />Bottom line: This phone gets it done with solid construction, big volume boost, tone control, and all the phone features you expect in one package.<br /><br />UPDATE: After using the phone for seven months now, my original impressions still stand.  This is a well made phone that gets loud enough for even the quietest calls.  Cons?  I've only found two: The speaker phone does not get very loud, which is a bit odd given the target hearing-impaired market, but it's not a major problem with the serious amplification available on the handset (you can actually use the handset as a speakerphone).  Second: I occasionally experience a bit of feedback with the handset, which can be quite loud.  The feedback seems to have more to do with handset position and high volume, as one would expect with high amplification, but it only occurs briefly and intermittently, so it is not a serious problem.  Overall a very good phone for the hearing impaired, and I'm happy with the purchase.ermittently, so it is not a serious problem.  Overall a very good phone for the hearing impaired, and I'm happy with the purchase.	\N	5	POSITIVE	5	5	\N	13591	132	\N	\N
