13790	I bought this mattress a few weeks ago and have been sleeping on it (on top of my &#34;normal&#34; mattress) since then---I do not have a medical condition that requires special treatment, but I just wanted something to increase the comfort factor of my base mattress, since I was frequently waking up with a creaky back, although my base mattress is still in good shape.  I had tried eggshell foam (OK but it retained heat like crazy), thick mattress toppers (ditto, plus they flattened quickly), and a much cheaper air mattress (Drive medical), which was great while it lasted, but it didn't last long (I also have a review posted under that product).  My goal was to improve mattress comfort without adding a heat sink, since I sleep hot as it is.  I had hesitated over the price of the item, but the first night I slept on the Roho convinced me it was worth the $---in fact I bought a 2nd one so I could cover my entire queen bed--the material the mattress is made of seems very sturdy, and it is smartly designed with snaps all around each unit (you receive 3 smaller units that snap together) so you can configure the connections in multiple ways.  I was going to wait to review until I'd used it for at least 1+ months so I could comment on durability, but I'm impressed enough to submit a review now.  One small temporary con--the mattress sections do have that plastic-y smell to them, but I just put them out in my backyard over the weekend and that pretty much took care of it.  I didn't notice any lingering plastic smell after I put it on my bed.  I've read in the other reviews that this mattress has been life-changing in many instances for people suffering from various medical conditions--which is great---but I also want to add that if you're just looking for increased comfort, it is an excellent investment!  Update:  as of July 2015, I have slept on the air mattress for 6 months and still do not have any leaks.  There's some normal slow air loss (as you would expect for 