14314	I purchased this item several months ago after finding it on sale. Since then I have used it regularly with decent results. Ideally I would give it 3.5 stars, but I'll round up to 4.   The good:  It seems to be made relatively well, though one of the foot pieces creaks when I use it (but I see nothing lose). The bottom of the curved bars has non-slip rubber on it so it will not slide around on hard floors.   The foot plates are a good size, big enough to accommodate larger feet, yet I have no problems with my smaller feet.   It does seem to work. It works in a similar way as a mini-stair machine, except the curved bottom makes the exercise a little wider, and the rocking motion adds a little bit of balance to it. I have never had any problems with this aspect of it, no feeling like I going to fall, though if you're worried about that you can always place a chair directly in front of you and hold on to the back of the chair for balance. It works my muscles, and if I get a good pace going it gets my heart rate up, too.   It's rather small and easy to store (as exercise equipment goes)I keep mine under my futon.     The bad:  The \\\\"mat\\\\" that it comes with it is useless. It's exactly the size the moonrocker needs it to be, but inevitably when I used it it moves a little to one side because of the rocking motion, and after that it catches the edge of the rug, pulling it up and getting in the way. Also, the rug is already coming apart from the repetitive motion of the wheels on it. I gave up and used it for a rug in front of my door (but hey, free rug!)   It comes with virtually no instructions, which is annoying (tip: press the button to alternate between the reps, timer and calorie counter, hold the button down to reset the reps and timer).  The rep counter is ridiculously sensitive. By this I mean it will have accumulated reps during shipping (mine registered over 3,000), and the slightest bump to one side will register as a rep. I don't use these myself so it isn't much of a bother to me.   If the battery in the counter were to ever run out I can see no way to replace it.   It's necessary to make sure the floor you will use it on is swept/vacuumed before use because if hair gets in the wheels on the bottom it's a pain to cut it out.     Overall it can be a useful addition to a workout routine, but it is far from a complete workout. It has a few problems, but it could be used to achieve good results. I would recommend this equipment to others, if they can find it on sale. For advanced fitness training, however, I would suggest a different piece of equipment as there is no way to increase the resistance, it's based on your own weight.	\N	3	POSITIVE	4	3	\N	14314	132	\N	\N
