14556	The vaporizer arrived with a minor flaw that was immediately resolved when I contacted the seller. Very prompt and nice service. The image of the vaporizer makes it look a bit clumsy so, as a pipe smoker, I was surprised that it fit so well in my hand. I am also delighted that it rests flat and steady on the tabletop when I set it down (another feature that pipe smokers notice).    I bought this item because I want to get away from inhaling cigarette smoke and I know that the worst tobacco toxins are released at high temperatures -- and high combustion temperatures are precisely what this device is designed to avoid. However, the low combustion also appears to lower the amount of available nicotine, so it will take some practice for practical use. That's the only reason it doesn't get 5 stars.    I find myself sometimes inhaling and then briefly holding my breath, in order to get the nicotine hit. Toking rather then smoking. I doubt that this is beneficial for my health. But there is generally no discernible smoke. And the flavor is very pleasant and sweet.    If too much flame is applied, it produces a minimal amount of smoke; something that the seller mentions in all honesty on their web site.    At this point, I don't know that this article will get me off cigarettes, but it is an interesting alternative. Especially for folks, like I, who find nicotine lozenges to be potent but expensive and unhealthy in their own way.    So far, I have tried vaporizing roll-your-own tobacco and some home-grown burley. I think my next step will be to find a good source of rustica tobacco (Nicotiana rustica) because it contains a high level of nicotine. Normally considered to be too strong for cigarettes (and even pipes) rustica could be the ticket for this vaporizer because I could then inhale virtually (or almost) smokeless and receive a higher content of nicotine.    All spoken like a true addict, I know, but I am enthusiastic about this device and I'm hopeful this technology will become even more effective in the future.    The bottom line is, do NOT expect the same level of gratification that would come from a cigarette. But DO expect this device to work. It does. If you have the willpower, you may be able to cross over to it, or you could use it as a transitional strategy for quitting.    For those who are using marijuana for truly medicinal purposes and are worried about the health effects of smoking, I believe you may find that your THC ingestion may be decreased, just as I have experienced with nicotine. However, it could be that THC vaporizes at lower temperatures (I'll leave the research to you). Still, you may want to invest in an electrically-controlled vaporizer for home use. Something that I find impractical for my application, but may be more effective for you.	\N	6	POSITIVE	4	6	\N	14556	132	\N	\N
