14674	The clinical data have been tallied and it's true:  Used correctly and faithfully, an oscillating electric toothbrush like this Oral B removes more plaque, slows the formation of tarter and strengthens the gums more effectively than a manual toothbrush.  Could it get any better?<br /><br />Well, yes. The Oral B 980TX comes with the original FlexiSoft head and the DualAction head, with its extra set of back-and-forth bristles.  The FlexiSoft head is the one in the main picture.  The longer interdental bristles jog loose debris caught between teeth.  The softness combined with the oscillating action massages the gums gently while reaching below the gumline to sweep away plaque before it can harden into tarter.<br /><br />The DualAction head combines the FlexiSoft's oscillating action with another set of bristles that waggle back and forth, a sort of pre-wash before the main scrubbing.  The result is an even more invigorating cleaning action.  The DualAction head is a bit larger than the FlexiSoft head but once you get used to it, you probably won't want to go back to the FlexiSoft alone.<br /><br />Alternatively, you could use different heads depending on the shape your mouth is in.  If this is your first electric toothbrush, you can expect a little bleeding as your gums toughen up, so brush for a couple weeks with the FlexiSoft head.  Then, switch to the DualAction and enjoy all the benefits of those added bristles.	\N	15	POSITIVE	5	15	\N	14674	132	\N	\N
