15236	This product is quite acceptable, but it doesn't match the specifications. For a start the colour is completely different to what is shown in most photos. It is a brown to black and is quite dark. This is fine for me, but far different to the tan flesh colour that was in most photos I have seen. The first photo I saw made me thing Tyler Knight was quite a pale caucasian dude! It is nowhere near 8.5 inches, unless you measure from the bottom of the suction cup to the top of the head. From the top of the head to the start of the balls it is 6 2/3 inches. Only just long enough to stop it popping out during play. But it is reasonably thick, has a nice shape and feels great.<br /><br />The futurotic material really is awesome and has the right combination of give and stiffness. It has a slight burnt rubber and vinyl smell which is nowhere near as bad as other similar toys I have owned. It doesn't (yet) burn when inserted as some of them have, often when they begin to emit an oily substance. It is said to be made of TPR, thermoplastic rubber. This is not very specific as it can cover a wide range of materials that melt and are rubbery. So it is difficult to predict how it will age. The material is quite sticky when not powdered so when washing after use, dry with a hair drier or lint free cloth and powder it with corn starch or futurotic brand maintenance powder, a small sample of which is included. And yes this will change the colour slightly so if that is an issue to you try to apply evenly and then dust with a soft paint brush. Do not put tissues or other linty type material on it as they will be quite difficult to remove without damage to the dong and keep it away from dust. You probably should keep it away from other plastics except the plastic sleeve it comes in. Other similar toys I have had tend to attack each other, shrink and deform and eventually form a sticky toxic smelling goop when kept in the same enclosed air space. The colour also tends to migrate.<br /><br />The vibrator isn't the most powerful or most quiet, I would rate it as adequate on both counts. The controller doesn't have a full off switch either, so you will want to remove the batteries after use. The wire from the controller goes into the base at side opposite the balls. The wires are not bonded to the material of the dong and there is a noticeable hole where they enter. I suspect that water could get in here and ruin the vibrator. The suction cup is completely useless. It can't stick to anything because it doesn't form a seal. It might hold inside a harness designed to hold suction cup dildos, but I don't have one so I can't say.<br /><br />All in all I would say it is a quite acceptable medium sized vibrating realistic dong. It didn't rock my world to be honest, but I would buy it again unless I found a better one, provided it ages well. Three stars.	\N	0	NEUTRAL	3	0	\N	15236	132	\N	\N
