16543	If you want it fast, the Melitta Fast Brew will take you from bean to brew in just a few minutes. The only machine I've experienced that is faster than the Fast Brew is the Bunn-O-Matic.  If you're looking for the best brewed coffee, however, look to another machine like the Cuisinart Grind and Brew. This machine extracts more flavor and body from the bean than the Fast Brew. I have experienced significant mechanical problems with the  Cuisinart Grind and Brew. In fact I bought and broke three of them in as many years. Twice for heat plate problems and recently because the grind motor burned up. That one was scary because I often set it up for auto brew.  But this is a review of the Melitta Fast Brew, so onward. As I mentioned before, the Fast Brew is fast. If it wasn't that would be a terrible name for it. I like the carafe. It is easy to pour from without any spills. The lid is tough to get off for cleaning. I also like the water meter on the outside front of the machine. I can easily see how much water I've added. Hint: Always use a filtered water source. The chlorine and other additives in most municipal water supplies is terrible when mixed with coffee beans. I also like the minimal space that it occupies on my kitchen counter. The area for pouring water into the machine is small and located adjacent to the coffee grounds. I haven't experienced any problem with spillage while filling the machine yet but I can see it happening one of these days in a rush to get my caffeine on!  I hate to use paper filters so I bought a No.4 permanent gold filter made by Maxwell House. It listed Melitta on the back as one of the machines that would accommodate this filter. Wrong! It doesn't fit into the coffee machine. I returned the filter and looked for another that would fit. No success. I ended up modifying the filter I had used on my Cuisinart Grind and Brew by carving off the top 1/4\\\\" with a razor blade. Be careful!  I use 3/4 cup of whole beans, ground for 15 seconds in ablade grinder. I know, not the right tool for the job. This makes a 12 cup pot of coffee. Actually, I'm thinking that I should back off on the water a little and make it a 11 cup pot because my grinder won't hold any more beans.   Finally, the conclusion to this review.  I would recommend the Melitta Fast Brew for someone who likes their coffee delivered fast. It makes a good cup of coffee. If you want the best brewed coffee, I would look around some more. If you do go for the Fast Brew, shop around. I picked mine up brand new for under $20.00.  If you want a permanent filter for your pot, be prepared to do some modifications, or perhaps the good people at Melitta have one specially made for this machine.  Enjoy. I've got to go now and refill my cup!	\N	8	POSITIVE	4	14	\N	16543	132	\N	\N
