16796	Like the other thermal massage bed sold by this company, if this bed actually does what it claims, and truly has \\\\"far infrared\\\\" it needs, by law, to have FDA clearance to be marketed in the U.S. as it emits thermal radiation and is a class II medical device under 21 CFR 80.5880. It is illegal, and dangerous, to market a device like this without FDA clearance as it may not perform as it claims or may actually be unsafe and can cause burns, electric shock, etc. The Safe Medical Devices Act of 1990 states you may not place such a device into commercial distribution until it is cleared by the FDA. According to all publicly available records (and these records are all available to the public) there is no record of this device having been so cleared. Amazon, and the seller, could be liable for significant damages in selling an uncleared and unregistered device, especially if it malfunctions and causes harm to someone. Unless you can get proof of FDA clearance such as a 510(k) clearance number and a device registration number (all cleared and registered medical devices have these numbers) it should be removed from the website.  No one should buy an uncleared device as you are taking a big risk. I have checked and this device is NOT cleared. The only way such a device would not have to be cleared is if it produced so little heat as to be completely ineffective and have no therapeutic value.  Either way, that's not something you want. There are actual thermal jade massage beds in the market that are FDA cleared such as the Ceragem and the ThermaJade. Yes, they cost more money - guess why. Don't waste your money on an unsafe or ineffective product.	\N	0	NEGATIVE	1	0	\N	16796	132	\N	\N
