17144	INSTRUCTIONS FOR USING THE GoWalking Body Fat Scale by Sportline  I bought mine in the 1990s at Walmart. I couldn't find a manual or the company on the internet. Here is what I found by hit or miss. I am hoping others find this useful. The scale works well except the little icons are hard to see and setup is confusing without the manual.  TO SET FOR A USER( settings for up to 10 people):  The 4 large buttons are (Top to Bottom):  ON/OFF  (on)  UP ARROW (up)  DOWN ARROW (down)  i (i)  1. Push on. you will see HELO [sic].  2. 1-10 will flash.  3. Push up or down to set your user number.  4. Push i quickly to get the little man/woman silhouettes on the left corners. Female is up on mine. This one you have to hit really quickly or it goes to the next setting. Up or Down to change man and woman icons.  5. Push i.  6. The number for cm for height will flash.  7. Push up or down to get ht. in cm. (inches times 2.54).  8. Push i (or it won't save it).  9. The number for your age will come on.  10. Push up or down to set age in years.  11. Hit i again.   12. When 0.0 flashes you can switch lb and kg by pushing the i button (not the arrows). The sign for kg is at the middle and lb at the bottom.  IF AT ANY POINT YOU GET LOST, TURN OFF AND START AGAIN. i WILL GO TO NEXT SETTING.       TO USE THE SPORTLINE GoWalking SCALE  1. Push on. See HELO [sic].  2. Hit either up or down once for last number. Hit more to change the number.  3. The number will stop flashing and the height in cm and male/female will display.  4. Then 0.0 will display.   5. Stand on scale with bare feet to get the body fat percentage, otherwise you get error messages, but the weight will briefly flash. It also helps if your feet are not too dry. Right when you step out of the tub is ideal. Also, being dehydrated, etc. will change your percentage.  6. Your weight will flash. Hitting i will toggle kgs(center) to lbs. (bottom).  7. The scale will calculate your body fat percentage using the impedance (resistance) between your two feet.   8. All this is based on tables of typical people. Men with a very high muscle mass sometimes need a better scale to get a true reading.	\N	18	POSITIVE	4	18	\N	17144	132	\N	\N
