17367	The best things about the splint were that 1) the item arrived before I even received the order status email - it was unbelievably fast; 2) it was packed well; and finally, 3) the credit back to my account was very prompt. Besides that, it was worthless. There were narrow straps and one wide strap with the splint versus 3 wide straps as in the photo. Although I measured my palm correctly so as to purchase the proper size, the contraption never fit properly. I guess it's possible that I have execeedingly fat arms in comparison to my hand but I doubt it. The straps were loose - as in they didn't attach to anything on the splint to hold them in place. So before I even climbed into bed, the straps would have already moved - sometimes off the splint and onto my arms or the other way and bunched up around my wrist. With nothing to hold them in place on the splint, of course they would move. You couldn't make them too loose or the splint would move all over my arm. Too tight and my arm was in pain from the hard plastic as well as throbbing and losing circulation. The only strap that really worked was the one that went across the palm and inside my thumb. And if by some freak chance the straps were in place when I fell asleep, they were all discombobulated when I woke up - again, either shoved up against my wrist/thumb or off the splint and on my bare arm. The straps had a little pad of velcro on the end that would adhere to anywhere else on the strap (or the splint - same fabric). But the problem with this design was that within a week of receiving these and attaching, reattaching and resizing the straps, the straps were starting to wear from the velcro adhering to them. What also didn't help was that I wore one of these on each of my wrists - bilateral carpal tunnel syndrome. So as I would be trying to attach the second one, the velcro on the straps from the second splint would catch and hold onto the first splint on my other arm. What a pain in the neck. This entire ordeal went on every night for a week when I finally said forget this and returned the splint. The online write-up (from a different website - not Amazon.com) made it seem like it was a really new innovative product not to be found in any corner drugstore and was the best night splint out there. Don't fall for it. After I went to the post office to ship it back, I stopped at my closest Walgreens and got a fantastic splint that doesn't move around my arm, is easier to attach, is comfortable, and was more than 50% cheaper of the product I just returned at the post office. Believe me, it was worth paying the 15% restocking fee to ship it back. It would have been cheaper if I never bought it. Oh and by the way, only one of the splints came with a single page instruction sheet filled with typos. Although I'm sure I could have figured out the splint without the sheet, I would have also thought I was doing something wrong with the splint if I didn't have it. It just couldn't be so simplistic or poorly designed or worth $50. Save your hard-earned cash and go to a local drug store or order a different one from Amazon.com.	\N	0	NEGATIVE	1	0	\N	17367	132	\N	\N
